Spec: clusterinfo

Purpose:
  Assemble the cluster-wide `clusterinfo` diagnostic payload: one fan-out of Kubernetes reads that
    collects the node roster, the cluster product distribution, the API server version, the running
    `vynil` version, the storage classes and the ingress classes into a @ClusterInfo — the complete
    "what cluster is this and what runs in it" answer per request. Everything is read live on every
    call — no cache, no auth check, no scrubbing inside this file.

References:
  ../dto.sdd — @ClusterInfo, @NodeInfo and @StorageClassInfo are the assembled output shapes; their
    wire keys and `null` rendering decide how each collected fact reaches the client.
  ../error.sdd — @DiagError::KubeError is the only failure lane any leg of this file can raise.
  ../state.sdd — the borrowed @kube::Client and the @Config.vynil_namespace string arrive from
    @AppState at /server/src/server.rs; this file builds no client and owns no namespace.
  ../anonymize.sdd — named to pin the boundary: unlike ./state.rs, ./vynilconfig.rs and ./logs.rs,
    this collector applies no scrub pass and returns no @ScrubStats; it depends on that file not at
    all (see Tasks).

Depends on:
  @kube `3.1.0` (/Cargo.lock) — the borrowed @kube::Client, @kube::Api via @Api::all and
    @Api::namespaced, @ListParams::default() on all four LIST verbs, plus the client-level fetches
    @Client::apiserver_version and @Client::list_api_groups.
  @k8s_openapi `0.27.1` (/Cargo.lock) — @Node, @StorageClass, @IngressClass and @Deployment (the
    last imported inside @get_vynil_version's body); only their metadata, status and spec fields are
    read, never mutated.
  @tracing `0.1` (/server/Cargo.toml) — the file's log lane; @get_vynil_version's `warn!` call is
    its single logging point.

Exposes:
  @get_cluster_info — the file's only `pub` item, reachable as
    @crate::collect::clusterinfo::get_cluster_info through `pub mod clusterinfo;` in ./mod.rs and
    `pub mod collect;` in /server/src/lib.rs; its lone call site is the /server/src/server.rs
    handler for item `clusterinfo`, which serves the @Ok payload through @axum::Json at `200`.
    Signature: `pub async fn get_cluster_info(client: &@kube::Client, vynil_namespace: &@str) -> @Result<@ClusterInfo, @DiagError>`
    Helpers, all private and observable only through that entry point: @get_nodes, @extract_roles,
    @detect_distribution, @get_apiserver_version, @get_vynil_version, @get_storage_classes and
    @get_ingress_classes.
  The six collected facts carried on @ClusterInfo, in assembly order:
    @ClusterInfo.nodes — @Vec<@NodeInfo> from the cluster-scoped @Node LIST, per node: @name, @roles
      (pushed order `control-plane`, `worker`, `infra`, default `node`), @instance_type, @arch, @os,
      @kubelet_version.
    @ClusterInfo.distribution — exactly one of the literals `GKE`, `EKS`, `AKS`, `OpenShift`,
      `Unknown`, from node labels first and @Client::list_api_groups second.
    @ClusterInfo.kubernetes_version — @Client::apiserver_version's `git_version`, verbatim.
    @ClusterInfo.vynil_version — @Option<@String>: the image tag segment of the first label-matched
      @Deployment in @vynil_namespace, or @None.
    @ClusterInfo.storage_classes — @Vec<@StorageClassInfo> from the cluster-scoped @StorageClass
      LIST: @name, @provisioner, @is_default.
    @ClusterInfo.ingress_classes — @Vec<@String> of @IngressClass names, cluster-scoped LIST,
      nameless items dropped.

Accepts:
  @client — a borrowed @kube::Client, cloned per leg into @Api handles only; no client is built, no
    credentials are read, and the caller's permission set (notably cluster-wide LIST rights) is
    exactly this file's visibility.
  @vynil_namespace — a `&@str` consulted once, as the @Api::namespaced target of the @Deployment
    LIST inside @get_vynil_version; never validated, never seen by any other leg.
  Nothing else: no selectors, field filters, limits, page knobs or per-item options — every LIST is
    @ListParams::default() over the whole collection.

Returns:
  @Ok of one @ClusterInfo with the six fields above, list order preserved as the API returned it —
    nothing here sorts, dedups, trims, case-folds or validates, and every label-derived value is the
    label's verbatim @String clone.
  @Err of @DiagError::KubeError carrying the failed leg's original @kube::Error unchanged —
    `DIAG-500`/`500` on the wire per /server/src/error.sdd — from the first hard-failing leg, with
    all later legs never attempted.

Raises:
  @DiagError::KubeError is the sole raisable variant, from five hard legs: the @Node LIST in
    @get_nodes, the second @Node LIST in @detect_distribution, @Client::apiserver_version, the
    @StorageClass LIST and the @IngressClass LIST — each mapped explicitly to @DiagError::KubeError
    via @map_err and `?`, with no retry, fallback or extra annotation.
  @DiagError::SerializationError never raises — the file serializes nothing, although the
    @get_cluster_info doc string claims failures "by serialization of the collected resources" (see
    Tasks).
  No panic path: absent names degrade through @unwrap_or_default and @filter_map; the file contains
    no @unwrap, @expect or explicit @panic.

Handles:
  Two soft legs degrade instead of failing: any @kube::Error from the @Deployment LIST is logged as
    the @tracing warn `Failed to get vynil version: ` plus the error @Display and answered
    @Ok(@None) — @get_vynil_version's @Err lane is unreachable; a @Client::list_api_groups failure
    is matched away silently and read as "not OpenShift".
  Absent names: @Node and @StorageClass @name become the empty string `""` entries, while a
    nameless @IngressClass is dropped from @ClusterInfo.ingress_classes entirely.
  Role extraction ignores values on `node-role.kubernetes.io/control-plane`,
    `node-role.kubernetes.io/master`, `node-role.kubernetes.io/worker` and
    `node-role.kubernetes.io/infra` (role labels are conventionally empty), but requires the value
    `master` on the legacy `kubernetes.io/role`; other values there contribute nothing, so plain
    workers land on the no-roles default `["node"]`. The legacy `master` case never duplicates a
    `control-plane` already earned from the node-role labels.
  Label value fallbacks, first hit wins verbatim: @instance_type tries `node.kubernetes.io/instance-type`,
    then `k8s.amazonaws.com/instance-type`, then `cloud.google.com/machine-type`; @arch and @os
    prefer `kubernetes.io/arch` / `kubernetes.io/os` and fall back to their `beta.kubernetes.io/`
    siblings; @kubelet_version exists only under @Node's @status @node_info, so a status-less node
    yields @None.
  Distribution scan order: for each @Node in list order, key presence only is tested —
    `cloud.google.com/machine-type` → `GKE`, `eks.amazonaws.com/nodegroup` → `EKS`,
    `kubernetes.azure.com/agentpool` → `AKS` — first matching node returns immediately; only when no
    node matches, any API group name ending `openshift.io` → `OpenShift`; else `Unknown`.
  Nodeless cluster: `nodes` is `[]`, cloud literals are unreachable, and `distribution` is decided
    by the API-group check alone.
  No authentication or authorization happens here — the /server/src/server.rs caller has already
    identified and admitted the request before this collector touches the cluster.
  The payload leaves unscrubbed: node names, label-derived facts and image references are emitted
    exactly as read, with no @ScrubStats and no `X-Diag-Redactions` path (see Tasks).

Must:
  A successful @get_cluster_info runs six legs in fixed sequential order — @Node LIST, second @Node
    LIST, @Client::apiserver_version, namespaced @Deployment LIST, @StorageClass LIST, @IngressClass
    LIST — awaiting each before starting the next, so the first hard failure aborts before
    subsequent legs are ever issued.
  The @Node resource is LISTed twice per successful call with identical @ListParams::default()
    arguments and no result sharing between @get_nodes and @detect_distribution.
  The four cluster resources (@Node, @StorageClass, @IngressClass cluster-wide via @Api::all) are
    read cluster-wide; only the @Deployment lookup is namespaced to @vynil_namespace via
    @Api::namespaced.
  @get_vynil_version inspects deployments only for the label check `app.kubernetes.io/name` equal to
    the value `vynil`; the first label-matched @Deployment in list order is the only inspected
    candidate — its first container's @image, taken second `:`-separated field verbatim as the
    version, then the loop breaks even when that candidate yields @None, so later labeled
    candidates are never examined.
  @ClusterInfo.kubernetes_version is the `git_version` text untouched — no `v` prefix handling,
    parsing or validation; an empty `git_version` ships as `""`.
  @StorageClassInfo.is_default is true exactly when the annotation
    `storageclass.kubernetes.io/is-default-class` equals the string `true`; absent or any other
    value is false, and @provisioner passes through raw.
  The file performs no secret collection or masking of any kind — no call into ../anonymize.rs
    exists (contrast the scrub lanes named in ../anonymize.sdd).

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover @extract_roles: control-plane via either node-role label with an empty value, the
      `["worker","infra"]` push order, the legacy `kubernetes.io/role: master` alias never
      duplicating control-plane, and `kubernetes.io/role: node` yielding only the default `["node"]`.
  [ ] Cover @get_nodes facts: the @instance_type three-key priority chain, `beta.kubernetes.io/arch`
      and `beta.kubernetes.io/os` fallbacks, @None @kubelet_version for status-less nodes, and the
      empty-string @name for a nameless @Node.
  [ ] Cover @detect_distribution: first-cloud-labeled-node-wins across `GKE`/`EKS`/`AKS`, the
      `openshift.io` suffix match on any group, `Unknown` for clean clusters and for a
      @Client::list_api_groups @Err, and that no cloud literal survives an empty @Node list.
  [ ] Cover the version legs: `git_version` passthrough, @vynil_version for every image shape pinned
      in the second-colon-field scenario — plain tag, registry-port, digest and the first-match
      `break` with a later tagged candidate skipped — the @Deployment-LIST @Err degradation to @None
      plus its warn line, and a hard-leg @kube::Error aborting later legs as @DiagError::KubeError.
  [ ] Cover list assembly: @StorageClassInfo.is_default only on literal `true`, the dropped nameless
      @IngressClass, the retained nameless @StorageClass entry, and API list-order preservation in
      every vector.
  [?] @Node is LISTed twice per call with identical parameters while @ClusterInfo discards the
      first result for the distribution pass, and all six round trips are awaited serially — one
      request costs up to six trips. Decide later whether the node list is reused and the six legs
      run concurrently.
  [?] @vynil_version reads the tag as the second `:`-separated field of the image: an untagged
      `registry:5000/vynil` reports `5000/vynil` and a digest-pinned `vynil@sha256:abcd` reports the
      digest `abcd` as the "version". Decide later whether proper image-tag parsing lands here.
  [?] @vynil_version takes the first label-matched @Deployment, reads only its first container, and
      then `break`s even when that candidate yields @None — a shared `app.kubernetes.io/name: vynil`
      label on another workload outranks the controller and no fallback scan exists. Decide later
      whether the lookup becomes a label-selector field query with candidate merge.
  [?] Soft-lane leniency is inconsistent: the @Deployment LIST failure logs a warn while the
      @Client::list_api_groups failure is swallowed with no log, so an RBAC-broken cluster answers
      `OpenShift`-absent identically to vanilla upstream; @get_vynil_version keeps a @Result
      signature it can never error through. Decide later whether the API-group failure is logged and
      whether the signature collapses.
  [?] @get_cluster_info's doc string promises propagated "serialization of the collected resources"
      failures the body never produces (nothing serializes here) and stays silent on both soft legs;
      the same doc block also opens with its `# Errors` section before the summary line. Decide
      later how the prose is corrected.
  [?] Nothing is scrubbed and no @ScrubStats travels with the answer, while /server/server.sdd
      carries the unqualified "Anonymize secrets in returned payloads" rule — node names,
      label-derived values and image references ship verbatim to any authenticated caller of this
      generic-tier item. Decide later whether clusterinfo belongs at the ../anonymize.sdd boundary.
  [?] Detection and reporting label sets disagree: distribution keys are
      `cloud.google.com/machine-type`, `eks.amazonaws.com/nodegroup` and
      `kubernetes.azure.com/agentpool`, but @instance_type has no Azure key — an AKS node reports
      @instance_type @None under @distribution `AKS`. Decide later whether one shared cloud-label
      table serves both scans.

Done when:
  Every Scenario below maps to a green test in `server`, the `[?]` decisions above are recorded, and
    `cargo test -p server` with clippy and fmt stays green.

Scenario: Roles are label presence not value
  Given a node carrying only `node-role.kubernetes.io/control-plane: ""`, one carrying both
    `node-role.kubernetes.io/worker` and `node-role.kubernetes.io/infra`, and one carrying only
    `kubernetes.io/role: node`
  When @extract_roles runs over them during the nodes leg
  Then their @roles are `["control-plane"]`, `["worker","infra"]` in that push order, and the
    default `["node"]`
  And a fourth node with only `kubernetes.io/role: master` yields `["control-plane"]`, while one
    with both that label and `node-role.kubernetes.io/control-plane` keeps `control-plane` once
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Fallback labels keep facts optional
  Given a nameless @Node whose labels hold only `k8s.amazonaws.com/instance-type: m5.large` and
    `beta.kubernetes.io/arch: amd64`, with @Node @status absent entirely
  When its @NodeInfo is built
  Then @name is `""`, @instance_type is `m5.large`, @arch is `amd64`, and @os plus @kubelet_version
    are @None serialized as explicit `null` per ../dto.sdd
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: First cloud-labeled node decides distribution
  Given a @Node list whose first item carries `cloud.google.com/machine-type` and whose second
    carries `eks.amazonaws.com/nodegroup`
  When @detect_distribution scans
  Then @ClusterInfo.distribution is `GKE` — the EKS-labeled node is never consulted
  But with the cloud labels only on the second node as `kubernetes.azure.com/agentpool`, the result
    is `AKS`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: OpenShift only after cloud misses
  Given a cluster whose every node has no cloud label
  When @Client::list_api_groups returns a group named `route.openshift.io`
  Then @ClusterInfo.distribution is `OpenShift` — a suffix test on the group name, not an exact-group
    lookup
  And when that call fails with a @kube::Error, the answer is `Unknown` with nothing logged,
    indistinguishable from a genuinely vanilla cluster
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Vynil version reads the second colon field
  Given a label-matched @Deployment whose first container image is `ghcr.io/vynil/controller:1.2.3`
  When @vynil_version extracts
  Then @ClusterInfo.vynil_version is @Some `1.2.3` verbatim
  And today's split reports @Some `5000/vynil` for the untagged `registry:5000/vynil` and @Some
    `abcd` for the digest-pinned `vynil@sha256:abcd`
  And when the first label-matched deployment yields no tag, the result is @None even though a
    later deployment with the same label carries `vynil:0.9`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Soft legs degrade the payload and hard legs abort
  Given the @Deployment LIST in @vynil_namespace is refused by RBAC while every other leg reads
    cleanly
  When @get_cluster_info runs
  Then it answers @Ok with @ClusterInfo.vynil_version @None and the warn line `Failed to get vynil
    version: …`, and one nameless @IngressClass is missing from @ClusterInfo.ingress_classes while a
    nameless @StorageClass still appears with @name `""`
  But when the @StorageClass LIST fails instead, `?` propagates @DiagError::KubeError as
    `DIAG-500`/`500` and no @IngressClass request is ever issued
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  @ClusterInfo body for a one-node EKS cluster:
    `{"nodes":[{"name":"ip-10-0-1-2","roles":["node"],"instance_type":"m5.xlarge","arch":"amd64","os":"linux","kubelet_version":"v1.29.9"}],"distribution":"EKS","kubernetes_version":"v1.29.9","vynil_version":"0.3.1","storage_classes":[{"name":"gp3","provisioner":"ebs.csi.aws.com","is_default":true}],"ingress_classes":["alb"]}`
  Soft-leg log body: `Failed to get vynil version: ` + the failed @kube::Error @Display — the file's
    only emitted log line.
